cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this work and the original data and method sources."
title: "Painter Street Overpass response analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Utpal
    affiliation: "Berkeley Seismological Laboratory, University of California, Berkeley"
  - family-names: Mosalam
    given-names: Khalid M.
    affiliation: "Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and Pacific Earthquake Engineering Research Center, University of California, Berkeley"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis of derived response measurements for 22 earthquakes
  recorded at the Painter Street Overpass during 2012-2024, with National
  Bridge Inventory inspection records. Reproduces response-feature screening,
  amplitude-dependent modal frequencies, and event-level persistent-shift
  tests. Response departures do not establish earthquake damage or its absence.
  This package starts from distributed derived measurements; it does not rerun
  waveform processing or modal identification. Code is MIT-licensed; original
  documentation, figures, and derived tables are CC BY 4.0, subject to source
  notices.
repository-code: "https://github.com/earthinversion/painter-street-analysis"
keywords:
  - structural health monitoring
  - bridge response
  - modal frequency
  - earthquake engineering
  - reproducible research
